TITLE:: ChipVCF
summary:: Virtual Analog Model of the Solid State Micro Technology SSM2044 4-Pole Low-Pass VCF
categories:: UGens>Filters
related:: Guides/Filtra, Classes/RolandOTA, Classes/Wasp, Classes/MS20Diode

DESCRIPTION::
ChipVCF is a virtual analog model of the classic SSM2044 4-pole (24 dB/octave) low-pass filter integrated circuit manufactured by Solid State Micro Technology, featured prominently in the Korg Polysix, Korg Mono/Poly, PPG Wave 2, and Crumar Bit 01/99 synthesizers.

The circuit features a 4-stage buffered differential ladder with an internal analog multiplier feedback gain cell. Unlike discrete transistor ladders, the SSM2044 incorporates an on-chip bass compensation network that reduces the dramatic low-frequency drop typical of classic ladders under high resonance. At resonance settings >= 1.0, the feedback loop stabilizes into a pure sinusoidal limit cycle with the characteristic biting "squelch" of early 1980s analog polysynths.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: freq
Filter cutoff frequency in Hertz (10 Hz to 0.49 * sampleRate). Supports audio rate and control rate. Default: 1000.0.

ARGUMENT:: res
Resonance parameter in [0.0, 1.2]. Self-oscillation occurs at res >= 1.0. Default: 0.0.

ARGUMENT:: drive
Overdrive factor (default 1.0, range [0.01, 20.0]). Controls input and inter-stage differential pair saturation.

returns:: An audio-rate filtered signal.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
s.boot;

// 1. Polysix Style Analog Bass Squelch
(
x = {
    var saw = Saw.ar([55, 55.3]) * 0.3;
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.01, 1.2), Impulse.kr(2));
    var cutoff = env.exprange(100, 4500);
    ChipVCF.ar(saw, freq: cutoff, res: 0.85, drive: 2.0) * 0.4 ! 2;
}.play;
)

// 2. Self-Oscillation Sine Melody
(
x = {
    var trig = Impulse.ar(0);
    var pitch = Demand.kr(Impulse.kr(4), 0, Dseq([440, 660, 880, 1100], inf));
    ChipVCF.ar(trig * 0.1, freq: pitch, res: 1.05, drive: 1.0) * 0.5 ! 2;
}.play;
)
::
